      "The volume that was bought by Augustus and the volume that is priced at seven and six are exactly one shelf apart in shelf order, in one direction or the other.",
      "The volume that is priced at two shillings is lower than an album of pressed ferns in shelf order.",
      "A treatise on clocks is exactly one shelf lower than the volume that was bought by Ottoline, with no shelf in between.",
      "The volume that was bought by Augustus is not priced at one and six. The volume that is priced at one and six is lower than the volume that was bought by Rodrigo in shelf order."
